  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ESAMI/trapca and Lund University 2023-2026, phase V - ESAMI/trapca 2023-2026, phase V</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">ESAMI/trapca and Lund University 2023-2026, phase V</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective is:

The trapca programme is expected to contribute to enhanced trade capacity towards increased regional economic integration and intra-African trade. 

The programme objective is:

Improved trade capacity in LDCs and low-income countries in sub-Saharan Africa to develop more efficient trade policy, trade law, trade facilitation, emerging trade related strategies and implementation and enforcement of negotiated regional, continental and multilateral trade outcomes.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Trapca&apos;s overall objective is to contribute towards poverty reduction through improved integration in the world economy by increasing knowledge/skills in Trade Policy among Least Developed Countries (LDCs) and Low-Income Sub-Saharan countries. In furtherance of this mandate, trapca has over the past sixteen years facilitated capacity building initiatives, professional networking and the sharing of information among the target countries. Lund University is the Academic Partner of ESAMI/trapca.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Trapcas &#xf6;vergripande m&#xe5;l &#xe4;r att bidra till fattigdomsminskning genom f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttrad integration i v&#xe4;rldsekonomin genom att &#xf6;ka kunskapen inom handelspolitiken bland de minst utvecklade l&#xe4;nderna och l&#xe5;ginkomstl&#xe4;nder s&#xf6;der om Sahara. Lunds universitet &#xe4;r ESAMI/trapcas akademiska partner.</narrative>
  </description>
